o.26:22 (בֶּטֶן), Wis.10:5, Sir.30:7, 2Ma.9:5 (6), al. ;] \nthe inward parts (heart, liver, lungs, etc.; Lat. viscera): Act.1:18. Metaphorical, of the seat of the feelings and of the feelings themselves (in Gk. poets, of anger, anxiety, etc.), the heart, affections (the characteristic LXX and NT reference of the word to feelings of kindness, benevolence and pity, is found in π.; see MM, xxiii; cf. Lft. on Php.1:8): 2Co.6:12 7:15, Phm 7 12 20, 1Jn.3:17; σ. οἰκτιρμοῦ, Col.3:12; σ. καὶ οἰκτιρμοὶ, Php.2:1; σ. ἐλέους θεοῦ; ἡμῶν, Luk.1:78; σ. Χριστοῦ Ἰησοῦ, Php.1:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":4846}],"occurrence_count":11,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sentimentos","count":5},{"gloss":"entranhas","count":1},{"gloss":"órgãos","count":1},{"gloss":"afeto","count":1},{"gloss":"afetos","count":1},{"gloss":"íntimos-sentimentos","count":1},{"gloss":"compadecer","count":1}]},"G4870":{"id":"G4870","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4870","disambiguated_id":"G4870 =","unique_id":"G4870","headword":"συνακολουθέω","transliteration":"sunakoloutheō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to accompany","definition_en":"συν-ακολουθέω, -ῶ \n [in LXX: 2Ma.2:4 2Mac 2:6 * ;] \nto follow along with, accompany: with dative of person(s), Mrk.14:51, Luk.23:49; before μετά, with genitive of person(s), Mrk.5:37.†\n (AS)","source_line":5022}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"seguisse","count":1},{"gloss":"seguia","count":1},{"gloss":"que-o-acompanharam","count":1}]},"G5415":{"id":"G5415","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5415","disambiguated_id":"G5415 =","unique_id":"G5415","headword":"Φορτουνᾶτος","transliteration":"Phortounatos","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Fortunatus","definition_en":"φορτούνατος (Rec. Φουρ-, see Mayser, 116 f.), -ου, ὁ \n (Lat.) Fortunatus: 1Co.16:17 (see Lft., Cl. Ro., 1Co., 59).†\n (AS)","source_line":5577}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Fortunato","count":1}]},"G95":{"id":"G95",